// Title: Powershell Defender Exclusion
// Sigma ID: 17769c90-230e-488b-a463-e05c08e9d48f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-04-29 | Modified: 2022-05-12
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects requests to exclude files, folders or processes from Antivirus scanning using PowerShell
//   cmdlets
// False positives:
//   - Possible Admin Activity
//   - Other Cmdlets that may use the same parameters
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-endpoint/configure-process-opened-file-exclusions-microsoft-defender-antivirus
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1562.001/T1562.001.md
//   - https://twitter.com/AdamTheAnalyst/status/1483497517119590403
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_defender_exclusion.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Add-MpPreference " or ProcessCommandLine contains "Set-MpPreference ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -ExclusionPath " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -ExclusionExtension " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -ExclusionProcess " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -ExclusionIpAddress ")
